{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791396454,"nonce":"kNwJOsgp7qRo9s9YXydkOk6HBy0=","title":"Cranelift: omit promotion probes when no native tier or reload can receive them","message":"With LLVM disabled (Tier2Backend::Cranelift) and hot reload off, install_promotion_requester already knows there is no optimizing tier, but Cranelift still emits entry count updates, per-loop hotness counters, request calls and helper-slot probes. TieredRuntime unconditionally forwards config.enable_osr. Interpreter-to-Cranelift OSR still needs resume helper generation; that is separate from emitting outgoing probes into baseline native code.\n\nObserved in NUC native code for integer reduction loops: shared HIR vectorization produces vpand/vpaddq, but the impossible native transfer paths force both vector counter and accumulator to spill/reload each iteration. SIMD regresses kernel52.9ms to89.3ms instead of closing the LLVM14.2ms reference gap. Trace /tmp/zyntax-counter-vector-native.trace, issue 2e204d8.\n\nGate outgoing native probes on a real LLVM destination or enabled hot reload; retain interpreter-first startup and interpreter baseline resume points. Apply the rule in TieredBackend construction and its setter so module installation cannot re-enable dead probes. Validate Cranelift-only interpreter OSR, LLVM promotion and hot reload; compare same-executable optional force-probe control and normal LLVM-off benchmarks, including wall time.","files":null}]}